> Hello All,
> One of the customers have an issue with starting X server on OSF/1 RT V1.3A (rev.112)
> Computer: DEC 3000 model 400 AXP
> Video adapter was changed due to failure from
> PMAGB-B to PMAGD-CA
> Now they are trying to start X server and receive something like:
> No video was found or driver loaded.

The owner's guide can be found here:
http://manx.classiccmp.org/collections/mds-199909/cd1/sys_opt/smfbpsgb.pdf

Seems like the PMAGD-CA aka ZLX-E3 needs at least OSF/1 V2.0 and
Open3D V2.4.
The ZLX-E3 is way more powerful than the PMAGB-B. I'm not sure if it
needs Open3D to run at all or if it only uses Open3D for advanced
3D functions. But if it needs it, you will have to check if you have
Open3D installed at all. It's a layered product that requires an extra
license key - or PAK (product activation key) as they are called here.

Dennis

